ple  will buy this story and buy  into it and it would be more universal  and for me i was like  this is universal this is my my son  my excuse me my nephew and my son they  look just like this little boy  and so that really um i got a pit in my  stomach to be honest mercedes when i was  told that and i said you know what  there's nothing like this out there in  the market  i'm going to do it myself i'm going to  do it my way because i know  that whether there's a black child on  the cover a spanish child on the cover  i mean an asian child on the cover this  is a story that resonates with everyone  you and i both know we always see those  stories on the news about those big  surprise  return homecomings right but it's the  story behind that  that this goes into i'm a little bit  deeper to pull back those layers so i  didn't care  um i i wanted to make sure that yes  my nephew was represented but there are  other books in the works i don't care  who's on the cover it's the story  behind it you know and i'm not going to  change the skin absolutely there's 1.2  million military children of active duty  members worldwide and representation  it does matter now tell us where can we  get  the book well the book i'm happy to  announce is  available on my website  talipavickers.com it's also  got picked up by barnes noble amazon  as well and you can also take it with  you on the go because it's an e-book too  as well  that it looks so great we have nellis  air force base here in las vegas i'm  sure  so many families could relate to the  story and again what an inspiring book  thank you for pushing for representation  because like i said it does matter  thank you so much talitha jc over to you
 

